 ## Overview
-This method extracts the initial geometric skeleton (vertices and edges) of a multi-resolution tetrahedral grid by exploiting its inherent regularity [S1]. It represents the grid as a union of parallel-plane sets, where planes sharing the same normal are grouped by their offsets [S1]. This approach efficiently identifies the topological structure of unstructured tetrahedral meshes without relying on local neighborhood searches [S1]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Adaptive Subdivision in DiffTetVR](807-adaptive-subdivision-in-difftetvr.md) and [DEFTET](6415-deftet.md) by using global linear algebra operations (Kronecker products and matrix inversions) to generate candidate vertices and edges in parallel via tensor broadcasting [S1].
